WEBVTT

asr-000018
00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:59.980
Senator Joel Villanueva: The budget briefing on the fiscal year 2027 proposed budget

asr-000019
00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:29.980
Senator Joel Villanueva: of the Department of Migrant Workers and its attached agencies is hereby called to order. I'd like to acknowledge, of course, the head of the department. It's always good to say that this is now a department, Secretary Hans Leo Cacdac, all our undersecretaries present here today, our OWWA Administrator PY Caunan,

asr-000020
00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:59.980
Senator Joel Villanueva: and the rest of our guests. I would also like to warmly welcome our friends from the Commission on Audit. And perhaps later, or perhaps at this point, may I request our Committee Secretary to acknowledge the other resource persons and guests present here today.

asr-000021
00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:12.460
Committee Secretary: Thank you, Mr. Chair. We would like to acknowledge the presence of our dear Secretary, Hon. Hans Leo Cacdac from the Department of Migrant Workers,

asr-000022
00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:24.500
Committee Secretary: Undersecretary Felicitas Q. Bay, by Foreign Employment Welfare Services, Asia-Pacific, Americas and European Affairs,

asr-000023
00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:35.700
Committee Secretary: Undersecretary Jainal Rasul, Jr., Policy and International Cooperation, Undersecretary Darlene Pajarito, Licensing and Anti-Trafficking in Persons,

asr-000024
00:10:36.140 --> 00:10:46.940
Committee Secretary: Undersecretary Dominique Rubia Tutay, Finance and Internal Management, Undersecretary Bernard Olalia, Adjudication Services and Regional Operations.

asr-000025
00:10:46.940 --> 00:10:53.940
Committee Secretary: From the Overseas Workers Welfare Administration, OWWA, we have Attorney Patricia

asr-000026
00:10:54.860 --> 00:11:05.980
Committee Secretary: Yvonne Caunan, Administrator. We also have Deputy Administrator Ryan Vincent L. Uy, Policy Development and Strategic Partnerships.

asr-000027
00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:16.280
Committee Secretary: We also have Deputy Administrator Rosalia Susana Bahia Catapang, Deputy Administrator for Operations,

asr-000028
00:11:17.080 --> 00:11:24.320
Committee Secretary: and Deputy Administrator-Attorney Jasmine Ann Gapatan, Administration and Fund Management.

asr-000029
00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:30.360
Committee Secretary: From the Commission on Audit, we have Attorney Cherry Ann Viernes Sula, Supervising Auditor,

asr-000030
00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:35.500
Committee Secretary: Ms. Regine Voloso, State Auditor 4, Audit Team Leader,

asr-000031
00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:39.740
Committee Secretary: Attorney Glyza Dimapilis Delapo, Audit Team Leader.

asr-000032
00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:49.340
Committee Secretary: From the Department of Budget and Management, we are joined online by Mr. Benjelit Suniga, Director 4.

asr-000033
00:11:49.340 --> 00:11:54.440
Committee Secretary: We also have Ms. Jessa Angara-Lavlin.

asr-000034
00:11:54.500 --> 00:12:03.220
Committee Secretary: Joyce Soriano, Jenna Vertulfo, Dulce de Vega, and April Ann Magsino, all from the Department of Budget and Management.

asr-000035
00:12:03.640 --> 00:12:05.100
Committee Secretary: That's all, sir.

asr-000036
00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:12.280
Senator Joel Villanueva: Thank you, ComSec, at maraming salamat sa bawat isa na nakapunta po sa araw na ito.

asr-000037
00:12:12.880 --> 00:12:14.620
Senator Joel Villanueva: Maikling pananilita lang po.

asr-000038
00:12:14.620 --> 00:12:23.200
Senator Joel Villanueva: Noong tayo po ay, siguro lahat naman nakakaalam na tayo yung nagsulong nitong Republic Act 11641,

asr-000039
00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:24.320
Senator Joel Villanueva: or the

asr-000040
00:12:24.500 --> 00:12:27.240
Senator Joel Villanueva: establishment of the Department of Migrant Workers Act.

asr-000041
00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:31.460
Senator Joel Villanueva: Personal po sa atin, ang tagumpay ng departamentong ito,

asr-000042
00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:38.300
Senator Joel Villanueva: kaya po every time we get an opportunity to look into this particular department,

asr-000043
00:12:38.540 --> 00:12:42.040
Senator Joel Villanueva: how we can improve because there's a saying, there's always room for improvement.

asr-000044
00:12:43.020 --> 00:12:47.000
Senator Joel Villanueva: Noong isinusulong po natin itong batas na ito, sinasabi po natin,

asr-000045
00:12:47.440 --> 00:12:54.140
Senator Joel Villanueva: nagtatayo tayo ng isang bahay, isang tahanan sa pamahalaan para sa ating mga bagong bayani.

asr-000046
00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:55.820
Senator Joel Villanueva: Sama-sama po natin,

asr-000047
00:12:56.420 --> 00:13:03.140
Senator Joel Villanueva: Pinagsama-sama po natin ang iba't ibang ahensya sa isang bubong at sa ilalim po ng isang accountable leadership,

asr-000048
00:13:03.940 --> 00:13:09.080
Senator Joel Villanueva: ang mga tanggapang dati ay hiwa-hiwalay ng pamahalaan.

asr-000049
00:13:09.080 --> 00:13:13.040
Senator Joel Villanueva: Hindi lamang po ito lipat bahay o pagpapalit ng karatula.

asr-000050
00:13:13.220 --> 00:13:16.140
Senator Joel Villanueva: It was a promise that wherever an OFW may be,

asr-000051
00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:24.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: there would be one government home ready to protect their rights and assist them from recruitment,

asr-000052
00:13:24.500 --> 00:13:25.700
Senator Joel Villanueva: to reintegration.

asr-000053
00:13:26.060 --> 00:13:29.720
Senator Joel Villanueva: I was looking at the fiscal year 2027,

asr-000054
00:13:29.960 --> 00:13:38.460
Senator Joel Villanueva: DMW and OWA have a combined proposed expenditure program of 11.615 billion pesos,

asr-000055
00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:45.620
Senator Joel Villanueva: which is 129.8 million or 1.1% lower than the previous year,

asr-000056
00:13:45.680 --> 00:13:48.040
Senator Joel Villanueva: which is this year, 2026 program.

asr-000057
00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:54.480
Senator Joel Villanueva: And of this amount, 7.267 billion will go to DMW OSEC,

asr-000058
00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:58.420
Senator Joel Villanueva: and 4.349 billion will go to OWA.

asr-000059
00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:02.660
Senator Joel Villanueva: Sa budget po para sa ating migrant workers,

asr-000060
00:14:03.340 --> 00:14:07.440
Senator Joel Villanueva: hindi po sapat na masabing nagagastos lamang ang pondo.

asr-000061
00:14:07.980 --> 00:14:13.480
Senator Joel Villanueva: Talagang ang tunay na sukatan ay yung pong kung may OFW bang naprotektahan,

asr-000062
00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:15.340
Senator Joel Villanueva: meron po ba tayong napauwi,

asr-000063
00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:17.740
Senator Joel Villanueva: meron po ba tayong nabigyan ng hustisya,

asr-000064
00:14:18.140 --> 00:14:20.940
Senator Joel Villanueva: at natulungan na makapagsimulang muli.

asr-000065
00:14:20.940 --> 00:14:23.520
Senator Joel Villanueva: And this becomes most urgent whenever,

asr-000066
00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:27.880
Senator Joel Villanueva: conflict erupts overseas.

asr-000067
00:14:28.420 --> 00:14:30.460
Senator Joel Villanueva: Sa tuwing may kaguluan sa Middle East,

asr-000068
00:14:30.580 --> 00:14:34.680
Senator Joel Villanueva: may OFW na naghahanap ng ligtas na matutuluyan,

asr-000069
00:14:34.860 --> 00:14:40.880
Senator Joel Villanueva: at may pamilyang naghihintay ng balitang makakauwi ng ligtas ang kanilang mahal sa buhay.

asr-000070
00:14:41.540 --> 00:14:45.520
Senator Joel Villanueva: Mayigit po isang milyong Pilipino ang nagtatrabaho sa rehyong ito,

asr-000071
00:14:45.520 --> 00:14:53.440
Senator Joel Villanueva: kaya po mahalagang patuloy po nating palaksin ang kahandaan ng ating departamento at ng OWA

asr-000072
00:14:53.440 --> 00:14:54.260
Senator Joel Villanueva: upang mabilis.

asr-000073
00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:58.080
Senator Joel Villanueva: At sapat na matugunan ang pangangailangan ng ating mga OFW,

asr-000074
00:14:58.080 --> 00:14:59.880
Senator Joel Villanueva: lalo na po sa panahong may krisis.

asr-000075
00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:17.900
Senator Joel Villanueva: Central to this response is the Action Fund. And the reports that this representation had received from July 2023 to July 2026, the fund assisted more than 606,000 OFWs.

asr-000076
00:15:17.900 --> 00:15:38.660
Senator Joel Villanueva: And from January to July of this year alone, it provided 2.95 billion pesos in assistance to 145,448 beneficiaries. And in response to the Middle East crisis, its 2026 funding was increased to 5 billion pesos.

asr-000077
00:15:39.260 --> 00:15:47.660
Senator Joel Villanueva: Sa likod po ng bawat numerong ito ay muli, isang OFW na nangangailangan ng pagpapagamot, ticket na pauwi.

asr-000078
00:15:47.900 --> 00:16:01.940
Senator Joel Villanueva: Agarang saklolo. And for 2027, the Action Fund must remain adequately funded and ready for both the daily needs of distressed workers and a possible large-scale crisis.

asr-000079
00:16:01.940 --> 00:16:16.940
Senator Joel Villanueva: Now, looking at OWWA's Emergency Repatriation Fund, the proposed funding is at 977.8 million, which is 24% lower than...

asr-000080
00:16:17.900 --> 00:16:30.440
Senator Joel Villanueva: than its 2026 allocation. Now, we must determine whether this can meet existing needs while preserving sufficient contingency capacity for, again, another emergency.

asr-000081
00:16:31.440 --> 00:16:46.700
Senator Joel Villanueva: Malinaw po that our OFWs have learned, have earned that assurance. In 2025 alone, they sent home a record 39.62 billion dollars, US dollars,

asr-000082
00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:53.140
Senator Joel Villanueva: personal remittances, supporting millions of families and strengthening our economy.

asr-000083
00:16:53.740 --> 00:17:06.880
Senator Joel Villanueva: Kaya po, dapat sikapin nating patibayin sa pamamagitan po ng budget na ito, ang bahay na sama-sama po nating itinaguyod at itinayo para sa kanila.

asr-000084
00:17:07.120 --> 00:17:15.880
Senator Joel Villanueva: Matatag ang pundasyon, sapat ang naglilingkod, bukas ang mga pintuan, at bawat piso ay may malinaw na patutunguhan.

asr-000085
00:17:17.120 --> 00:17:17.880
Senator Joel Villanueva: Nasusukat din

asr-000086
00:17:17.900 --> 00:17:26.300
Senator Joel Villanueva: ang resulta at OFW na tunay na natutulungan saan mang lugar na naroon sa mundong ito.

asr-000087
00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:43.300
Senator Joel Villanueva: Muli, marami pong salamat. At this juncture, I will give now the floor to our good secretary, our good friend, Department Secretary Hans Leo Cacdac for his presentation.

asr-000088
00:17:43.740 --> 00:17:44.500
Senator Joel Villanueva: Sir, you have the floor.

asr-000089
00:17:45.480 --> 00:17:47.880
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Maraming salamat po, Mr. Chair.

asr-000090
00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:56.900
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Sir, Senator, isa po kayong tinatanaw namin bilang isa sa founding fathers and mothers of the DMW.

asr-000091
00:17:57.160 --> 00:18:05.900
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kung meron pong Mount Rushmore kaming itatayo sa DMW, Mr. Senator, kasama po kayo doon sa aming Mount Rushmore of Founders.

asr-000092
00:18:07.120 --> 00:18:16.900
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At maraming salamat po sa inyong pagtanaw ng aming mga achievements and at the same time areas of improvement, ang aming kakulangan ng resources.

asr-000093
00:18:17.900 --> 00:18:26.680
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: 37 billion po ang aming pino-propose at 11.602 nga po ang iginawad ng NEP.

asr-000094
00:18:26.680 --> 00:18:45.700
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Now, hindi po kami nagre-reklamo dahil malinaw po sa kabinete na ang aming direktiba at pinag-agrihan sa pong kabinete ay umayon po sa determinasyon ng ating mahal na kagawaran ng DBM.

asr-000095
00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:47.700
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At ang Pangulo...

asr-000096
00:18:47.900 --> 00:18:51.920
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ang nagpapasinaya ng ating budget sa pamahalaan.

asr-000097
00:18:52.060 --> 00:19:02.100
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kaya kami naman po ay aayon sa mga nakatalaga sa National Expenditure Program with some room for proposing.

asr-000098
00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:08.320
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At ito naman po ay aming nakakoordinate din po mismo sa ating mahal na Pangulo.

asr-000099
00:19:08.820 --> 00:19:13.880
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: The President is well aware of our overall needs.

asr-000100
00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:16.020
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And that which can still be allocated.

asr-000101
00:19:16.740 --> 00:19:17.880
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: In addition...

asr-000102
00:19:17.900 --> 00:19:19.580
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: To the National Expenditure Program.

asr-000103
00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:23.920
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, yun po ang mga iuulat namin sa inyo.

asr-000104
00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:30.240
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Pero si Yusek Niki, tutay po ang mag-pre-present.

asr-000105
00:19:30.460 --> 00:19:40.440
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Gusto ko lang po bago i-rekomenda na ipasa kay Usec Nikki ang hapag ay gusto ko lang banggitin muli yung Action Fund.

asr-000106
00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:44.720
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ang dami po nating natulungan, Mr. Senator.

asr-000107
00:19:45.060 --> 00:19:47.820
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At alam nyo rin po ito na iuulat ko rin sa inyo.

asr-000108
00:19:47.900 --> 00:19:51.760
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, daman-dama po mga OFWs talaga.

asr-000109
00:19:52.760 --> 00:19:56.360
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Itong Action Fund na alam naman po natin inyong isinaisip.

asr-000110
00:19:57.100 --> 00:20:05.900
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Itong Action Fund po ay bunga po ng inyong pagod at hirap na witness ko po ito mismo nung itinatalaga ang kagawaran.

asr-000111
00:20:07.280 --> 00:20:09.740
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At gusto ko pong iulat sa inyo, Mr. Senator.

asr-000112
00:20:09.740 --> 00:20:15.040
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Because of the Action Fund that you had so instituted.

asr-000113
00:20:15.580 --> 00:20:16.740
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ay andami po mga OFWs.

asr-000114
00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:21.260
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Over 100,000 ang nakatanggap ng financial assistance.

asr-000115
00:20:22.300 --> 00:20:27.260
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: 20,000 ang legal assistance na nakatanggap.

asr-000116
00:20:27.640 --> 00:20:33.460
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Meron po tayong 25 legal retainers.

asr-000117
00:20:34.600 --> 00:20:37.200
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At hindi po ibig sabihin yan mga abogado.

asr-000118
00:20:37.200 --> 00:20:38.500
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kundi law firms.

asr-000119
00:20:38.860 --> 00:20:41.680
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, with 4 or 5 lawyers per law firm.

asr-000120
00:20:42.140 --> 00:20:47.200
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Higit-kumulang at least 100 lawyers ang tumutulong sa ating mga OFWs.

asr-000121
00:20:47.900 --> 00:20:48.900
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: All around the world.

asr-000122
00:20:48.900 --> 00:20:51.900
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Especially in the places where they are most present.

asr-000123
00:20:51.900 --> 00:20:53.900
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: In the Middle East and in Asia.

asr-000124
00:20:53.900 --> 00:20:59.900
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And meron din tayong around 12 in-house lawyers.

asr-000125
00:20:59.900 --> 00:21:03.900
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, meron tayong internal and external counsels.

asr-000126
00:21:03.900 --> 00:21:06.900
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Sa medical, ganun na rin po.

asr-000127
00:21:06.900 --> 00:21:12.400
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ganun na lamang po ang pasasalamat ng mga OFWs na tulungan natin.

asr-000128
00:21:12.400 --> 00:21:17.300
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: By way of example, meron tayong mga cancer patients na unfortunately,

asr-000129
00:21:17.300 --> 00:21:20.300
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: naging hurub or undocumented sa Middle East.

asr-000130
00:21:20.300 --> 00:21:24.300
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Pero dahil sa Action Fund, nakauwi po sila.

asr-000131
00:21:24.300 --> 00:21:27.300
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Nabayaran ang kanilang kautangan sa ospital.

asr-000132
00:21:27.300 --> 00:21:29.300
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Stage 4 cancer.

asr-000133
00:21:29.300 --> 00:21:33.300
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Nakauwi at nakapiling ang kanilang mga pamilya sa kanilang huling sandali.

asr-000134
00:21:33.300 --> 00:21:36.300
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At ganun na lamang malungkot na sila ay nasawi.

asr-000135
00:21:36.300 --> 00:21:42.300
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: But ganun na lamang ang pasasalamat ng pamilya at mismo ng OFW bago siya yumao.

asr-000136
00:21:42.300 --> 00:21:46.300
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Dahil kahit papano kapiling niya ang kanyang pamilya sa kanyang huling sandali.

asr-000137
00:21:46.300 --> 00:21:53.300
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ehemplo lamang po ito ng ating mga natutulungan.

asr-000138
00:21:53.300 --> 00:22:01.300
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Meron din po tayo nabibigyan ng tulong pinansyal sa mga nagsasagawa ng compassionate visits.

asr-000139
00:22:01.300 --> 00:22:06.300
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So halimbawa po, kung covered ng insurance ang compassionate visit,

asr-000140
00:22:06.300 --> 00:22:13.300
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: ang tanong po ay paano yung sustento po ng isang wife na dumadalo sa kanyang OFW husband sa ICU.

asr-000141
00:22:13.300 --> 00:22:15.300
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Pagsustento, basic needs.

asr-000142
00:22:15.300 --> 00:22:18.300
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Yun po doon pumapasok ang Action Fund.

asr-000143
00:22:18.300 --> 00:22:27.300
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At ganoon na lamang ang kapanatagan ng kalooban ng mga pamilya, knowing na nakakadalaw sa abroad sa ICU,

asr-000144
00:22:27.300 --> 00:22:32.300
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: nagbabantay sa ICU sa kanilang mahal sa buhay ang ating mga OFW families.

asr-000145
00:22:32.300 --> 00:22:36.300
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ehemplo lang po ito among other things, Mr. Senator.

asr-000146
00:22:36.300 --> 00:22:39.300
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Dahil yan din po ang gusto ng ating mahal na Pangulo.

asr-000147
00:22:39.300 --> 00:22:40.300
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Direct impact.

asr-000148
00:22:40.300 --> 00:22:44.300
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Itong Action Fund should have a direct impact on the lives of our OFWs and their OFW families.

asr-000149
00:22:45.300 --> 00:22:48.300
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kung mamarapatin ninyo po, Mr. Senator.

asr-000150
00:22:48.300 --> 00:22:51.300
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: I will request our good USEC Nikki.

asr-000151
00:22:51.300 --> 00:22:57.300
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And of course, time also for our dear Admin PY to make our presentation.

asr-000152
00:22:57.300 --> 00:22:59.300
Senator Joel Villanueva: Yes, thank you very much, Secretary Hans.

asr-000153
00:22:59.300 --> 00:23:06.300
Senator Joel Villanueva: And I remember distinctly when we were establishing or pushing for this bill to become a law,

asr-000154
00:23:06.300 --> 00:23:09.300
Senator Joel Villanueva: the establishment of the Department of Migrant Workers,

asr-000155
00:23:09.300 --> 00:23:13.300
Senator Joel Villanueva: we really looked into this particular funding,

asr-000156
00:23:13.300 --> 00:23:15.300
Senator Joel Villanueva: this item of Action Fund.

asr-000157
00:23:15.300 --> 00:23:20.300
Senator Joel Villanueva: And I'm happy to note that it is serving its purpose,

asr-000158
00:23:20.300 --> 00:23:23.300
Senator Joel Villanueva: especially in taking care of our migrant workers.

asr-000159
00:23:23.300 --> 00:23:26.300
Senator Joel Villanueva: We give the floor to USEC Nikki,

asr-000160
00:23:26.300 --> 00:23:29.300
Senator Joel Villanueva: the former USEC of DOLE,

asr-000161
00:23:29.300 --> 00:23:31.300
Senator Joel Villanueva: now USEC of DMW.

asr-000162
00:23:31.300 --> 00:23:34.300
Senator Joel Villanueva: That's why we're having a hard time with DOLE.

asr-000163
00:23:34.300 --> 00:23:36.300
Senator Joel Villanueva: We'll give the floor to USEC Nikki.

asr-000164
00:23:36.300 --> 00:23:38.300
Senator Joel Villanueva: Please, you have the floor, ma'am.

asr-000165
00:23:38.300 --> 00:23:40.300
DMW Undersecretary Dominique Rubia-Tutay: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-000166
00:23:40.300 --> 00:23:42.300
