Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: So how do we go about na i-push natin ito? Ito sa mga tinatawag nating makabagong bayani at alam naman natin kahit na noong pampanahon ay nagkagewang-gewang na ekonomiya ng mundo, nagkaroon ng world crisis, lumulutang-lutang pa rin tayo dahil nandiyan po yung ating mga OFWs na nakapack up, nakasuporta sa atin through their remittances.

asr-001374
01:20:40.400 --> 01:20:48.080
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Ngayon, kailangan nila natin tulong through the DMW and OWA. Siguro naman, we really need to support.

asr-001375
01:20:49.220 --> 01:20:58.160
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: The DMW and OWA na sila nagkaalaga sa ating mga OFWs. So how do we go about pagdating sa budget deliberation? May ibigay itong 2 billion?

asr-001376
01:20:58.160 --> 01:21:08.940
Senator Joel Villanueva: Yes, tama po kayo. Record high yung pinapadala ng OFWs na 39.62 billion US dollars in personal remittances.

asr-001377
01:21:08.940 --> 01:21:19.200
Senator Joel Villanueva: Ang sa atin lang po ay alam nyo naman how budgeting works when you increase the budget of a particular agency or increase.

asr-001378
01:21:19.220 --> 01:21:27.020
Senator Joel Villanueva: The budget of an item here, we have to find out saan natin na po pwedeng kuhanin.

asr-001379
01:21:27.200 --> 01:21:38.680
Senator Joel Villanueva: Isa po kanina dun sa napag-usapan nga natin, isa sa nakita natin kanina, Senator Rafi, merong nilagyan ng pondo yung personal services pero wala namang item.

asr-001380
01:21:38.680 --> 01:21:47.040
Senator Joel Villanueva: So mukhang hindi nila mapapakinabangan yung dinagdag na pondo dun sa OWA dahil wala namang item, wala namang plantilya.

asr-001381
01:21:47.040 --> 01:21:57.760
Senator Joel Villanueva: So that's 200 million already, but according to our friends from OWA, kung malabas naman yung plantilya, kaya nilang punan ito.

asr-001382
01:21:57.920 --> 01:22:14.620
Senator Joel Villanueva: So we'll find ways and of course with your help and the support of Senator Javis, our finance chair, he gave me assurance that he will join us later on today as we look into the budget of DMW and OWA.

asr-001383
01:22:14.620 --> 01:22:16.840
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Okay, thank you. Dalawang tanong na lamang.

asr-001384
01:22:17.040 --> 01:22:37.760
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Mr. Chair, Sec. Hans, doon po sa mga seafarers natin na ayaw maglayag dahil doon sa mga drone strikes, natakot sila, ayaw nilang pumalaot, ito mga tripulanting ito, anong tulong ang pwedeng maibigay sa mga ito?

asr-001385
01:22:39.460 --> 01:22:46.380
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Yes po, ang bilang po natin, Mr. Senator, Mr. Chair, is 1,500 po.

asr-001388
01:22:46.680 --> 01:22:55.000
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: In the last three years, na itinalaga natin yung issuance natin, pagkilala ng right to refuse sailing, 1,500 po ang nag-manifest.

asr-001389
01:22:55.340 --> 01:23:05.580
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: However, Mr. Senator, nakalagay po doon sa 1,500, nakalagay po sa rules natin on right to refuse sailing, they should not be discriminated against.

asr-001390
01:23:06.620 --> 01:23:16.020
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At ang magandang balita po dito, the 1,500 who have been reported to us and affirmed by their respective license mining agencies, hindi naman po silang pinagbabawalan.

asr-001391
01:23:16.020 --> 01:23:34.080
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, as far as we know, wala pong naapekto hang nag-exercise ng right to refuse sailing dahil marami naman pong rota ang mga shipping lines at they are just merely transferred from one voyage, one assignment to another.

asr-001392
01:23:35.220 --> 01:23:44.980
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: But having said that, yun pong mga umuuwi ay binibigyan po natin ng action fund benefit as they come home, Mr. Senator.

asr-001393
01:23:46.020 --> 01:23:59.940
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Second, saan pa mas mga kamura tayo yung marami tayong tie-up sa mga different hotels partners natin kapag may mga dumarating ng mga OFWs before they are sent back to their homes in the provinces?

asr-001394
01:24:00.620 --> 01:24:11.080
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: So, chine-check-in sila sa tulad ng kabayano, hotel and all other hotels versus kung tayo ay magtayo ng mga accommodation houses.

asr-001395
01:24:11.540 --> 01:24:15.840
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Kasi paano kung puno yung hotel at that time dumating ng mga OFWs, marami sila, kunyari 20 eh.

asr-001396
01:24:16.020 --> 01:24:17.960
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Wala na palang room na available.

asr-001397
01:24:18.780 --> 01:24:28.920
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Kung tayo ay magtatayo ng sarili natin mga accommodation houses para sa mga repatriated OFWs papunta probinsya, which one sa tingin ninyo mas more practical?

asr-001398
01:24:29.180 --> 01:24:32.260
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Yung mag-tie-up sa mga hotel o magpatayo tayo ng mga accommodation houses?

asr-001399
01:24:32.260 --> 01:24:36.020
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ako pong tingin ko po dyan at ito lumabas na yung issue neto ng COVID.

asr-001400
01:24:37.180 --> 01:24:43.900
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kung ang scale po ng repatriation is a global pandemic o a global conflict, global crisis,

asr-001401
01:24:44.060 --> 01:24:45.900
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: kung saan libo o daang libo

asr-001402
01:24:46.020 --> 01:24:50.660
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: ang umuuwi, mainam po na yung private sector po ang mag-handle.

asr-001403
01:24:50.760 --> 01:24:55.320
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Yung hospitality sector who has greater expertise sa pangangalaga ng tao.

asr-001404
01:24:55.420 --> 01:24:56.900
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Katulad nung nangyari po sa COVID.

asr-001405
01:24:57.680 --> 01:25:06.140
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At hindi po kaya ng gobyerno na magtayo ng accommodation with let's say 1,000, 2,000, 10,000 rooms.

asr-001406
01:25:06.780 --> 01:25:09.420
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Wala po yan sa linya ng trabaho ng gobyerno.

asr-001407
01:25:09.520 --> 01:25:12.580
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: I think in the past, sinubukan na po yan, government-run hotels.

asr-001408
01:25:12.580 --> 01:25:15.820
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At eventually, tinurn over din po sa private sector.

asr-001409
01:25:16.020 --> 01:25:24.320
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: However, Mr. Senator, Mr. Chair, ay pwede naman po sa tingin ko, kasi ginawa na rin po ng OWA ito,

asr-001410
01:25:24.680 --> 01:25:30.700
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: pwede naman po magpatakbo itong plano na rin ni Admin PY ito, ng smaller scale.

asr-001411
01:25:30.940 --> 01:25:38.840
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So halimbawa, kung 50 rooms, 25 to 50 rooms, pansamantalang paglalagyan, pwede naman po yun.

asr-001412
01:25:38.960 --> 01:25:43.360
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Pero on a bigger scale, sa tingin ko po, hindi kaya ng pamahalaan ito.

asr-001413
01:25:43.360 --> 01:25:44.320
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: It's not sustainable.

asr-001414
01:25:44.320 --> 01:26:01.700
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At ang katapusan po niyan, Mr. Senator, Mr. Chair, ay magre-reklamo rin po yung mga tao na hindi nasa antas ng hospitality sector standards ang pangangalaga sa kanila.

asr-001415
01:26:01.820 --> 01:26:08.320
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So sa tingin ko po, on a smaller scale, yes, pwede po hawakan ng DMW o ng OWA.

asr-001416
01:26:08.320 --> 01:26:14.320
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Pero kung pangmalawa ka na po ito, sa tingin ko, the private sector is best suited.

asr-001417
01:26:14.420 --> 01:26:15.360
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: to take care of them.

asr-001418
01:26:15.420 --> 01:26:21.180
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kabayan Hotel, most notably, has been a foremost lodging space for them.

asr-001419
01:26:22.160 --> 01:26:26.540
